{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision","id":1339543,"title":"Exalted 3e Weapon Revision","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-05T00:21:02-07:00","id":1339543,"title":"Exalted 3e Weapon Revision","content":"While I liked the idea of weapon tags in 3e, I felt that the version that we got in the core book wasn't ideal. When Scion 2e came out, I was introduced to the idea of each weapon having a budget of points to spend on tags, so that each weapon was balanced against each other.<br /> <br /> I've taken that idea and applied it to the weapons in Exalted. I hope that you find it helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JKed54gYEYSEMmf4OUw_2E9ctKQLcCHSWAjsvCgMXYE/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JKed54gYEYSEMmf4OUw_2E9ctKQLcCHSWAjsvCgMXYE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JKed54gYEYSEMmf4OUw_2E9ctKQLcCHSWAjsvCgMXYE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JKed54gYEYSEMmf4OUw_2E9ctKQLcCHSWAjsvCgMXYE/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T02:23:43-07:00","id":1339553,"title":"","content":"Haven't read it yet but my exact thought when i connected on the forum page was &quot;I'd really like something a bit different about weapons&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T05:35:47-07:00","id":1339575,"title":"","content":"Question about stunning: is it supposed to knock you out at <i>any</i> level of damage? Cos if so that seems a bit powerful. <br /> <br /> &quot;It's ok, I incapacitated the deathlord with my slingshot&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T09:36:38-07:00","id":1339616,"title":"","content":"Is Fixed meant to cost 4?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T09:44:36-07:00","id":1339618,"title":"","content":"Yeah and then you have &quot;negative&quot; tags which gives you more points to buy it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T09:45:10-07:00","id":1339619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision?p=1339575#post1339575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about stunning: is it supposed to knock you out at <i>any</i> level of damage? Cos if so that seems a bit powerful.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's ok, I incapacitated the deathlord with my slingshot&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Stunting means that when the target arrives at 0 hp he is stunned and not dead","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:01:04-07:00","id":1339624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision?p=1339618#post1339618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah and then you have &quot;negative&quot; tags which gives you more points to buy it</div> </div> </div> </div>Flame Piece<br /> Archery(Short) 0<br /> Lethal 0<br /> Blast 1 <br /> Blatant -1 <br /> Fixed 4<br /> Slow -1<br /> <br /> Firewand (Lethal Melee with Bayonet, Bashing otherwise)<br /> Archery(Short) 0 <br /> Melee 1<br /> Lethal 0 <br /> Blast 1 <br /> Blatant -1 <br /> Fixed 4 <br /> Slow -1<br /> Two-handed -1<br /> <br /> Huh, ok. I get it.<br /> <br /> Not sure about Blatant as a tag, I'd nix it to make Fixed cost 3. Or possibly make Fixed cost a variable amount Fixed (1) adds 1 instead of the user's Strength, Fixed (5) adds 5?<br /> <br /> I feel like The Burning Name really shouldn't be based on Strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision?p=1339619#post1339619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stunting means that when the target arrives at 0 hp he is stunned and not dead</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is different from Bashing... how?<br /> <br /> Otherwise... I really like this. Still tempted to give shields the two weapon Clash bonus when paired with any other weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-05-2019, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:34:38-07:00","id":1339629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision?p=1339624#post1339624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flame Piece<br /> Archery(Short) 0<br /> Lethal 0<br /> Blast 1<br /> Blatant -1<br /> Fixed 4<br /> Slow -1<br /> <br /> Firewand (Lethal Melee with Bayonet, Bashing otherwise)<br /> Archery(Short) 0<br /> Melee 1<br /> Lethal 0<br /> Blast 1<br /> Blatant -1<br /> Fixed 4<br /> Slow -1<br /> Two-handed -1<br /> <br /> Huh, ok. I get it.<br /> <br /> Not sure about Blatant as a tag, I'd nix it to make Fixed cost 3. Or possibly make Fixed cost a variable amount Fixed (1) adds 1 instead of the user's Strength, Fixed (5) adds 5?<br /> <br /> I feel like The Burning Name really shouldn't be based on Strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is different from Bashing... how?<br /> <br /> Otherwise... I really like this. Still tempted to give shields the two weapon Clash bonus when paired with any other weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really not sure. The problem is the document references &quot;stunning damage&quot; opposed to I guess Bash and Lethal, but it's not explained anywhere.<br /> <br /> My guess is it's supposed to to lethal damage, but assures you not to kill your victim. But I don't know if it's the intention of the author.<br /> <br /> Blatant as a tag seems fine to me, it represents the fact this weapon is not suited to ambush someone and no one else knows it. I think it's fine.<br /> <br /> I think Fixed could be adapted but he just decided to reuse the value for the flamegun. Actually I think he created this tag this way solely for the purpose of conceiving the logical Flame Piece with slow and Blatant, but Fixed and Blast, which makes sense to me<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:57:17-07:00","id":1339635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339543-exalted-3e-weapon-revision?p=1339629#post1339629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blatant as a tag seems fine to me, it represents the fact this weapon is not suited to ambush someone and no one else knows it. I think it's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitting someone with a sledgehammer isn't exactly silent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:11:02-07:00","id":1339641,"title":"","content":"Yeah but with a FireArm it's even less silent. The point is the weapon makes sound &quot;by nature&quot;, if you had a hammer infused with Red powder to pake it &quot;PSHIIIIIIIIIIIIT&quot; when you hit something with it I guess you could add the Blatant tag","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:21:05-07:00","id":1339649,"title":"","content":"Might just be a case of coming up with enough tags to make firewands work. <br /> <br /> &quot;Shit, I'm one short, uh.... They go BOOM! And it's obvious! That'll work.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:37:03-07:00","id":1339655,"title":"","content":"I've rewritten Stunning to be a bit more clear about what it means. It's a guarantee that no matter how hard you hit someone with this weapon, they won't die unless you want them to.<br /> <br /> I've left Fixed at 4 damage because weapon choice shouldn't completely replace buying Strength 5. That's also why I made cost 4 points, so that there is always a downside to choosing a weapon that lets you neglect Strength.<br /> <br /> I wanted Shield to be an action tag that stands on its own instead of throwing a bunch of smaller effects together. After all, now that having the Shield tag isn't a downside (and there isn't a Flexible tag to just ignore it) more types of weapons can benefit from having it. The advantage of bucklers/target shields/tower shields is that they a source of the Shield tag that can't be disarmed. You could still get the clash bonus if you wielded a shield by itself Captain America Style.<br /> <br /> Blatant is a tag that has thus far gone on ranged weapons and is intended to make them less suitable for Stealth builds. The contrast is between bows and slings for sniping as opposed to flamedust weapons. In a modern setting, most guns would have the Blatant tag to simulate the sound of the gunshot and how forensics can identify bullets/guns. For a melee weapon, the equivalent would be less a sledgehammer and more a lightsabre (forged from frozen lightning?), emitting a continuous hum when unsheathed, shedding bright light, and leaving easily identifiable wounds.<br /> <br /> I separated Flame into Blast, Blatant and Fixed so that I didn't have multiple tags that did similar things like Crossbow and Flame did in the core book, and to make the effect more granular. I wanted people to be able to use the tag system without having to come up with more tags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:17:11-07:00","id":1341282,"title":"","content":"Blatant does seem like a bit too &quot;free&quot; right now. You typically don't find yourself rolling to notice an attack anyway. If you want to make it less suitable for stealth builds, maybe have it so that all ambushes (negating defense) are treated as surprise (-3 defense) instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:18:52-07:00","id":1341283,"title":"","content":"That may be something best left to storyteller adjudication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T15:13:18-07:00","id":1341716,"title":"","content":"Blatant is a tag I adapted from Scion 2e. It's let about forewarning and more about the aftermath. If you shoot someone with a firewand there will be a flash of light, a fwoom, and distinctive burn marks. You can still sneak up on someone with it.<br /> <br /> Maybe getting rid of ambush would be a good idea to make in fit in Exalted more, and it would be a pretty strong downside.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, I've made that change since it fits better with the Exalted ruleset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","user":"Indivisible","date":". 10-16-2019, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}